# Esc cancels a prompt (it used to do nothing), the footer names it, and the
# model picker offers "Other…" near the top. The settings page and the wizard
# share these prompts; this drives the wizard, since a journey should not
# drive the full settings page (see e2e/README.md). Leaving the settings page
# with "Saved N changes" is covered by TestPrintPageSummary.

[!pty] skip 'no pseudo-terminal here (/dev/ptmx will not open)'

exits 130 pty-run -wait 'Which coding agent' -send '\r' -wait 'Conversation mode' -send '\r' -wait '(?s)Other… \(type a model id\).*esc cancel' -send '\x1b' -- nav-pilot config setup
stdout 'esc cancel'
stdout 'Cancelled\. Nothing was written\.'
! exists home/config.toml
